  "query_preview": "..\nThe monsoon trough remains to our north and west late this afternoon\nwith drier weather prevailing across the Marianas. Drier conditions \nwill persist for another day or two before the monsoon trough sags \nsouthward. Shower and thunderstorm chances will begin to increase on \nSaturday with scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms possible \nas early as Saturday evening and likely continuing through the \nweekend and into next week. Model guidance differs significantly on \nthe potential development of Invest 92W with much uncertainty in the \nforecast around the middle of next week. Regardless, residents of the\nMarianas should continue to monitor the forecast over the coming \ndays and anticipate increasing wind, shower coverage, and \nthunderstorm chances around the middle of next week.",
